Git Basic Workflow:
Today I learned the basic Git workflow and how Git tracks changes in a project.

## What is Git?

Git is a Version Control System (VCS) used to track changes in source code and manage different versions of a project.

## 1. Git Init

Creates a new Git repository in the current project.

```bash
git init
2. Git Status
Shows the current state of files in the working directory.

git status
It shows modified, untracked, and staged files.

3. Git Add
Moves files from the working directory to the staging area.
Add a specific file:
git add filename
Add all files:
git add .

4. Git Commit
Saves the staged changes as a commit in the local repository.
git commit -m "Initial commit"
The commit message describes what changes were made.

5. Git Config
Used to configure the Git username and email.
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"
Check configuration:
git config --list

6. Git Log
Shows the history of commits.
git log
It displays the commit ID, author, date, and commit message.

